    "Model tends to overestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after recent spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Mean reversion is strong in the 7-14 day horizon; forecasts should be adjusted downward if prices remain above 1.5σ above the 30-day moving average.",
    "Overshoots after spikes (e.g., +5%+ above peak) should be capped at 1.2x the peak value to avoid overcorrection.",
    "Sentiment = 0.00 implies no directional bias — forecasts should be anchored to recent 18-day average, not extrapolated.",
    "In the 15-30 day horizon, model often underestimates downward trends — apply a 0.5–1.0% downward bias if true outcome shows >2 consecutive days of decline.",
    "If true outcome deviates >3σ from historical mean, re-evaluate model’s volatility assumption and adjust forecast range accordingly."
  ]
